# Production safety — Cursor must follow this

- Never deploy or promote a plain checkout of `main` to production.
- Never run `vercel --prod`, `vercel promote`, or reassign the production domains
  unless the user explicitly asked to ship and you own the release.
- Pushing Git changes is not permission to deploy them.
- The live release contains preserved Workspace, Calendar, Tasks checkout,
  Templates, Courses, pricing, and contact overlays that are not all present in
  a plain Git tree.
- Use a preview deployment for review. Before production, compare against the
  current live deployment and preserve every existing overlay.
- Run the guarded release/preflight checks and verify both domains after release.
- `sheetomatic.com` and `workspace.sheetomatic.com` must always point to the same
  verified release.
- Known-good preserved deployment on 22 Oct 2026:
  `dpl_2C3TEUHc4fVjnaYwJKGMe8utX4Ls`.
- If another agent is releasing, do not compete. Hand off the tested commit and
  wait for the release owner.

This ID is a checkpoint, not a permanent pin. Follow docs/PRODUCTION_FORWARD_BASELINE.md; never run automatic newest-READY alias pinning or overwrite a newer verified release.
